# Rule: Android Implementation

This rule constrains how the FitMate Android app is implemented with React Native, Expo, and TypeScript.

## Tech baseline (locked by DEC-001, DEC-016)

- Stack: React Native + Expo + TypeScript. Do not introduce Flutter, Kotlin, Swift, Capacitor, or Ionic.
- Navigation: **Expo Router** (file-based, native-stack built-in). See DEC-016.
- Sheets: @gorhom/bottom-sheet.
- Icons: lucide-react-native. Stroke width 2.
- Storage: @react-native-async-storage/async-storage behind typed, account-scoped adapters; `expo-secure-store` for refresh/session secrets. Access tokens stay in memory.
- Gestures/Animation: react-native-reanimated + react-native-gesture-handler.
- SVG/Vector: react-native-svg (for ring progress, icons).
- Date/Time: @react-native-community/datetimepicker (native).
- Toast: reuse the existing `mobile/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx`; do not add a second toast dependency.
- Image picker: expo-image-picker.

## Dependency governance

- Treat the versions pinned in `mobile/package.json` as the active baseline. Never take package versions from an old tutorial or prototype document.
- Prefer an existing dependency, then an Expo SDK module, then a React Native platform API, before proposing a third-party package.
- Before adding a third-party dependency, record the feature need and check active maintenance, current Expo/React Native New Architecture compatibility, release recency, security history, license, native/bundle cost, accessibility, and meaningful community adoption. Popularity alone is insufficient.
- Do not add deprecated, archived, abandoned, web-only, legacy bridge-only, or peer-dependency-incompatible libraries.
- Do not add overlapping navigation, UI-kit, icon, sheet, gesture, animation, storage, form, or state libraries. Reuse the approved stack.
- Do not install or upgrade packages automatically. Under the current workflow, provide the user an exact `npx expo install <package>` command and explain why it is needed; implementation may not claim compatibility until the user supplies verification output.
- Do not mass-upgrade dependencies while converting a screen. Isolate dependency changes and preserve the lockfile.

## Project layout

- All mobile code lives under `mobile/`. The web folder (`src/`) is **content baseline only** (fields, validation, role behavior) and must not be modified.
- **Do not** import web modules from `src/` into `mobile/`. The two codebases are separate.
- **Do not** copy theme tokens, CSS class names, or component styles from web into mobile (DEC-004, DEC-015).
- `mobile/app/` for Expo Router file-based routes (RootStackProvider at `app/_layout.tsx`).
- `mobile/src/theme/` for tokens (`tokens.ts`) and `ThemeProvider.tsx`.
- `mobile/src/components/ui/` for primitives (Button, Card, Chip, Input, Avatar, Toast, BottomSheet).
- `mobile/src/features/<feature>/` for screens grouped by domain.
- `mobile/src/services/` for API transport, authentication, storage, and feature service interfaces/adapters.
- `mobile/src/mocks/preview/` for deterministic development-preview fixtures only. Preview fixtures are never production fallbacks. Avatar placeholders must NOT reuse unlicensed URLs from the web prototype (DEC-017).
- `mobile/src/utils/` for pure helpers (BMI calculator, calorie math, time formatters, toxic filter).
- `mobile/src/navigation/` for any cross-cutting navigation helpers (deep-link mapping, linking config).

## TypeScript

- Strict mode on (tsconfig strict: true).
- Every screen exports its props type and reuses the service types.
- No `any` unless absolutely necessary; if used, add a comment explaining why.

## Production service pattern

- Read `docs/design/stitch-react-native-rules.md`, `docs/production/contract-baseline.json`, and the backend OpenAPI before changing a service.
- UI consumes typed feature services/hooks; it does not call arbitrary endpoints or store wire DTOs directly in presentation state.
- Generate or map wire types from the recorded OpenAPI revision. Preserve unknown/null and exact enum casing.
- Use local/staging backend configuration only during development. Never call production or paid providers without explicit operator approval.
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` may contain a public base URL or non-secret presentation setting only; never credentials or signing/provider/model keys.
- Fixtures are allowed only in an explicit `__DEV__` design preview. API failure never falls back to fixtures or fake success.
- Remove `RewardSimulation`, demo credentials, mock AI responses, and client-generated financial results from production execution paths.
- AI providers are backend-only and capability-gated. The app never calls Gemini or loads model artifacts directly.

## Permissions

- Image picker (camera/library): request on demand; if user denies, show fallback to pick from library or skip.
- Request camera, gallery, and notification permissions only when the released feature needs them, with a denial/fallback path. Do not request broad permissions on startup.
- Storage permission: not needed (AsyncStorage is app-sandboxed).

## Android-specific behavior

- Safe area: use react-native-safe-area-context on every screen.
- Status bar: dark icons on the approved light background. Configure globally in `app/_layout.tsx`.
- Hardware back: handled by native-stack + bottom-tabs automatically. For sheets, use the sheet library hook.
- Font scaling: must work up to 1.5x without clipping. Verify in MOB-200.
- Min touch target: 48x48dp. Verify in MOB-200.

## Anti-patterns

- Do not use inline styles for tokens. Always reference the theme.
- Do not read AsyncStorage directly from a component. Always go through a service or storage helper.
- Do not place business logic in screens. Extract to utils or services.
- Do not import web modules from src/ into mobile/. The two codebases are separate.

## Verification before declaring a task DONE

- Type-check passes (npm run type-check).
- Lint passes (npm run lint).
- Acceptance criteria in docs/mobile-redesign/acceptance-checklist.md for the relevant phase PASS.
- Visual regression: at least one sanitized screenshot on Android emulator for each representative layout/state.
- Task is updated in docs/mobile-redesign/tasks.md (status, commit link, notes).
- Commit exists only when the user explicitly authorized it. A commit is not evidence that runtime verification passed.

## Release

- Do not run EAS production builds, upload to Google Play, purchase services, or contact production systems without explicit user/operator authorization. Release gates are tracked by MOB-808 and backend BE-826/827.
